ield-8/eeaf296f318adb017c70b6f62719ecd0e364769a3d8fc39897b9337866681e1c" "q-334055/field-8/a7bd601d0dd3398ee151f162242eecc6ed6e4f542f69ea528f6598d41a0c5ff8" "q-334055/field-8/ec1653609f9cebb62a9913800a35eab2f57eeb9ad18a35c0b0659acc83abb280"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-334055"] :question/problem "For the polynomial $f(x)=8{x}^{4}-2x+1,$ show that $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$We say $f(x)$ is of order $g(x)$ as $x\\to a,$ and we write \n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nif there exist {{field-1}} constants $K$ and $\\delta $ such that\n\n$$\n{{field-2}}\\,\\text{for all}\\,0<|x-a|<\\delta .\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we need to show that\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nBy the triangle inequality,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & \\le {{field-5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let $|x|<\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then, the best upper bound we can form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & <{{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|f(x)|\\le 3$ whenever $|x|<\\frac{1}{2}.$ Thus, taking {{field-7}} and {{field-8}} satisfies the definition, and we conclude that $f(x)=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We say $f(x)$ is of order $g(x)$ as $x\\to a,$ and we write \n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nif there exist $\\text{positive}$ constants $K$ and $\\delta $ such that\n\n$$\n|f(x)|\\le K|g(x)|\\,\\text{for all}\\,0<|x-a|<\\delta .\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, in our case, we need to show that\n\n$$\n|f|\\le K\\cdot 1\\,\\text{for}\\,0<|x|<\\delta \n$$\n\ni.e.,\n\n$$\n|f|\\le K\\,\\text{for}\\,0<|x|<\\delta .\n$$\n\nBy the triangle inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & =|8{x}^{4}-2x+1| \\\\  & \\le |8{x}^{4}|+|2x|+|1| \\\\  & =8|x{|}^{4}+2|x|+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let $|x|<\\frac{1}{2}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & =|8{x}^{4}-2x+1| \\\\  & \\le 8|x{|}^{4}+2|x|+1 \\\\  & <8{|\\frac{1}{2}|}^{4}+2|\\frac{1}{2}|+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & <3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|f(x)|\\le 3$ whenever $|x|<\\frac{1}{2}.$ Thus, taking $K=3$ and $\\delta =\\frac{1}{2}$ satisfies the definition, and we conclude that $f(x)=O(1)$ as $x\\to 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334055/field-3" "q-334055/field-4" "q-334055/field-5" "q-334055/field-6" "q-334055/field-7" "q-334055/field-8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-1/f8414cbebe64635b9a2cffa962e807207e3a93393f6a9dc622f8a4dbe5b99827" :answer/id #uuid "1d224f08-f1e5-5fb9-9f0a-80aadc6f920a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "real" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-1/eea192e3dc06faf49b4c58da817f24997dbe963b134e653e268085daf71b8667" :answer/id #uuid "3d71ee32-f941-5ebc-80ce-2ead4743a65d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "positive" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0892dc2b-fbf8-5ee3-b23d-5b639e9a88de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334064/field-1/eea192e3dc06faf49b4c58da817f24997dbe963b134e653e268085daf71b8667" :answer-field/choices ["q-334064/field-1/f8414cbebe64635b9a2cffa962e807207e3a93393f6a9dc622f8a4dbe5b99827" "q-334064/field-1/eea192e3dc06faf49b4c58da817f24997dbe963b134e653e268085daf71b8667"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-2/264dfd89ef7ef3d70f8031df8f0ecfded99c79bea8d5020cc0770343c4f6e4c5" :answer/id #uuid "a335f7d0-7fe0-5492-b4ab-f3a1ad3c00a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(x)\\ge Kg(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-2/fd854f678999d3a7c6ed6443df3f388c5ce9fc63318d6a89bf28361806bf3f5f" :answer/id #uuid "8f750d0c-c6ad-57ba-8026-50cb21301c62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|f(x)|\\le K|g(x)|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-2/5fd1b269b6311d1e38717dc5795357f9bfdee0582b6ad7f81d5a706648519612" :answer/id #uuid "fb9334d2-693a-52