ld/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334064/field-8/8b8de1b43584597170b98057b044f717dc2ba20cfa00e11a688796b2582527ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-334064/field-8/4d0fb41fb67d5c03a99c990997495ad71d7aa8699a5ab83e955fb86c0cd5821f" "q-334064/field-8/f5380a2721094d9c7562aa3ed09773af1a36691f0fc6abc707e063c28d0b519b" "q-334064/field-8/8b8de1b43584597170b98057b044f717dc2ba20cfa00e11a688796b2582527ac"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-9/409800b9e4aa6d60fdbb6cd42f25fde2821cf681a21c845328a030eeb838af16" :answer/id #uuid "4e8e6874-45df-53e8-bd8c-10073c9f46aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\delta =4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-9/eeaf296f318adb017c70b6f62719ecd0e364769a3d8fc39897b9337866681e1c" :answer/id #uuid "5938ad42-5e9a-5fc5-9773-473f20843394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\delta =1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-9/ec1653609f9cebb62a9913800a35eab2f57eeb9ad18a35c0b0659acc83abb280" :answer/id #uuid "1ed46dca-1423-5cf9-873e-42e35e31e488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\delta =\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064/field-9" :answer-field/id #uuid "58cb3e3d-20c1-5306-9a25-98921adba7e1" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334064/field-9/eeaf296f318adb017c70b6f62719ecd0e364769a3d8fc39897b9337866681e1c" :answer-field/choices ["q-334064/field-9/409800b9e4aa6d60fdbb6cd42f25fde2821cf681a21c845328a030eeb838af16" "q-334064/field-9/eeaf296f318adb017c70b6f62719ecd0e364769a3d8fc39897b9337866681e1c" "q-334064/field-9/ec1653609f9cebb62a9913800a35eab2f57eeb9ad18a35c0b0659acc83abb280"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334064" :question/id #uuid "b8c0eabe-c032-59c7-8dc3-d9808369162b" :question/math-academy-id "q-334064" :question/problem "For the polynomial $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+x,$ show that $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$We say $f(x)$ is of order $g(x)$ as $x\\to a,$ and we write \n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nif there exist {{field-1}} constants $K$ and $\\delta $ such that\n\n$$\n{{field-2}}\\,\\text{for all}\\,0<|x-a|<\\delta .\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we need to show that\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nBy the triangle inequality,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & \\le {{field-5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let $|x|<1.$ Then, we have {{field-6}}, and the best upper bound we can form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & \\le {{field-7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|f(x)|\\le 4|x|$ whenever $|x|<1.$ Thus, taking \n\n$$\n{{field-8}},\\,{{field-9}}\n$$\n\n satisfies the definition, and we conclude that $f(x)=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$" :question/worked-solution "We say $f(x)$ is of order $g(x)$ as $x\\to a,$ and we write \n\n$$\nf(x)=O(g(x))\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nif there exist $\\text{positive}$ constants $K$ and $\\delta $ such that\n\n$$\n|f(x)|\\le K|g(x)|\\,\\text{for all}\\,0<|x-a|<\\delta .\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, in our case, we need to show that\n\n$$\n|f(x)|\\le K|x|\\,\\text{for}\\,0<|x|<\\delta .\n$$\n\nBy the triangle inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & =|3{x}^{2}+x| \\\\  & \\le |3{x}^{2}|+|x| \\\\  & =3|x{|}^{2}+|x|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $|x|<1,$ then we have $|x{|}^{2}<|x|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n3|x{|}^{2}\\le 3|x|.\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|f(x)| & \\le 3|x{|}^{2}+|x| \\\\  & \\le 3|x|+|x| \\\\  & =4|x|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|f(x)|\\le 4|x|$ whenever $|x|<1.$ Thus, taking $K=4$ and $\\delta =1$ satisfies the definition, and we conclude that $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334064/field-1" "q-334064/field-2" "q-334064/field-3" "q-334064/field-4" "q-334064/field-5" "q-334064/field-6" "q-334064/field-7" "q-334064/field-8" "q-334064/field-9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00e4f805-bb4c-51d9-be19-acc3021667c1"] :knowledge-point/q