" "q-335445/field-3/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335445/field-3/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-4/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" :answer/id #uuid "57e1d75c-ed1c-5f1f-8b06-f74f690c6008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" :answer/id #uuid "edcca080-8fde-5a68-a475-177d3ccbcb6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-4/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer/id #uuid "522b77b0-05d5-54c4-a0fc-105385ee30cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "99cbf787-e718-59fb-b2ab-4df5f7a11a16" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335445/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" :answer-field/choices ["q-335445/field-4/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" "q-335445/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" "q-335445/field-4/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer/id #uuid "16b57961-32f5-5cd4-8c94-878c63c6c7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer/id #uuid "b1f376e8-38b1-5b8a-a981-de385508e306" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer/id #uuid "26edda93-794e-5bc2-ba59-ad3bb12fc036" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "ab1fde28-e6af-5704-8174-7dad9e9db494" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer/id #uuid "6aec5de7-f312-5a91-bf12-3c37369d945d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e512a2-f362-576f-8e70-f593d950f9c8" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335445/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer-field/choices ["q-335445/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335445/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335445/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335445/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" "q-335445/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335445" :question/id #uuid "ac4293b7-4265-5467-bc7b-b86d5611daed" :question/math-academy-id "q-335445" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2+{e}^{-x},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(2+{e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,{e}^{-x}=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(2)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{2+{e}^{-x}}_{⏟}}_{f}),\n$$\n\nand this is true by the $\\text{reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2+{e}^{-x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x}=O(2).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines   $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and the  $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(2).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(2)\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335445/field-1" "q-335445/field-2" "q-335445/field-3" "q-335445/field-4" "q-335445/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335445"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-1/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer/id #uuid "9b6535e3-9b3a-5763-925c-6ff919ad41d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-1/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer/id #uuid "042e5e5f-9163-5450-b60f-e571b964ef32" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-1/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer/id #uuid "3a7753e5-8f9d-5303-a33a-6ce60c4b1d20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-1/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer/id #uuid "9732a179-e270-5883-a7d0-c1e6023b7a53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-1/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "f69450f5-3826-5ec4-9395-3addde505008" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "089540ee-6911-5a87-8b20-930cfe6299aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335071/field-1/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer-field/choices ["q-335071/field-1/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335071/field-1/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335071/field-1/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335071/field-1/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4