" :answer/id #uuid "4315727b-bbe0-515b-9424-32c0bfeb4791" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-3/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer/id #uuid "7bc7a0db-3678-5299-8c5b-ade27636101c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "b772cbac-ab48-5b85-a560-0c19c60b2c28" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335071/field-3/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer-field/choices ["q-335071/field-3/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" "q-335071/field-3/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335071/field-3/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335071/field-3/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335071/field-3/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-4/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" :answer/id #uuid "e02bfad2-bbaa-5529-9ce2-5d495cf282d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-4/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" :answer/id #uuid "811a26be-6de9-512e-a7ae-42a733c69318" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" :answer/id #uuid "0f585a8a-9b61-5618-aafe-0a5ce320ef44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "c29a584f-5796-56db-b609-531eeaff29f0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335071/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2" :answer-field/choices ["q-335071/field-4/e04811e52d1b108844992320b02362618b439dac20ffc031cd3e9eda4c7aaa2b" "q-335071/field-4/4aba6ae530a1a9ae6a0e811a31dd556956a43739e9518d9a3cb43c8ffe3000ae" "q-335071/field-4/124b0c2eb11420d91f7684989e46375a3c1c904a04910b2d823439550b297bf2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "9d49d62d-3171-54ed-829e-5b8164e0d4b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer/id #uuid "c7e4974d-1594-5af6-b2aa-0fb4f34e7faa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer/id #uuid "491ddb23-1835-5387-becf-e8a79fdffbd9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" :answer/id #uuid "3495262f-ed50-5b4b-8be5-00cdb7ed6da1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer/id #uuid "485056da-64ab-53c7-a5e8-cb9070c020a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "34e35d80-0d12-57f7-8154-318fb39ebee5" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-335071/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810" :answer-field/choices ["q-335071/field-5/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" "q-335071/field-5/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" "q-335071/field-5/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" "q-335071/field-5/cc545c04e2dcad28fd649be5b590cd32108605dca0f2f8781f99422c4ab67505" "q-335071/field-5/438b4c4d03a21de630e66c77197769846fa4a0ad2f925cfdb3df140268e70810"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-335071" :question/id #uuid "54e0af89-1e9b-5900-bf6e-4113ca0cfa32" :question/math-academy-id "q-335071" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=2{e}^{4x}+x,$ then $f=O({e}^{4x})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{x}{2{e}^{4x}})=0$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,x=O(2{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(4{e}^{4x})$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O({e}^{4x})$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-2}}  \nand  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation.\n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each selected step.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand this follows by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n2{e}^{4x}=O(2{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx=O(2{e}^{4x}).\n$$\n\nSince $f=2{e}^{4x}+x,$ by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=2{e}^{4x}+x=O(2{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x})=O(4{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nwhich justifies line $\\text{L4}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(4{e}^{4x}),\n$$\n\nand by $\\text{the constant multiple property}$ with $c=4,$ we conclude\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{4x}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-335071/field-1" "q-335071/field-2" "q-335071/field-3" "q-335071/field-4" "q-335071/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-335071"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-335438/field-1/747bf59f129b39ed16d0609e880083b7ec7fa22b98988114d7cffd9bba5b175a" :answer/id #uuid "eef891e4-ad80-5e5e-a2e9-61c0b8ef6780" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the sum property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335438/field-1/8fd8091ad80f7d2511ea6ab5fad6d1dd366029d679ddf5d03fdce7b5b86d2f68" :answer/id #uuid "67bbbdaa-4331-54b2-b8d3-05938de37e1b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335438/field-1/3fbc166f0ca82f98a387364d8e9c36034073c6b33cb86f09819bccc9f55bb35c" :answer/id #uuid "debf6873-0622-578b-b420-859033d3d8c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-335438/field-